      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 4,250 mg dose is also far above the maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **425 mg PO three times daily.** This isn't a standard tablet strength, so it's less likely.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n\nPlease tell me the dose you intended. If 4,250 mg is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. I'd still recommend a pharmacy review first."
      }
