      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin has no therapeutic use. It's well into the range where lactic acidosis becomes a serious risk, and that risk applies to a patient with normal kidney function too. Entering it would put an order in the system that could reach the patient.\n\nYou have other ways to proceed:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that right away, for example metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or whatever dose you choose.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If you believe there is a real clinical reason for this dose, a pharmacist or your institution's high-alert or override process should review it. That process should also document your reasoning.\n- **Check for a different intent.** If you meant a different drug, a different strength, or a total daily dose, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
